      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely understandable that you feel hopeless when the effort feels futile, but the desire to connect with your former self is a powerful, albeit painful, sign of your inner fight. Even when things feel hollow, small anchors—like a specific scent, a piece of music, or a sensory experience—can sometimes create tiny points of connection. Please remember that even in the fog, the part of you that is reaching out and asking for help is still very much alive.",
      "source": "target",
